  @case 'height: what the odd primes of a ratio cost, over the coords that name them'  [pure]  @ 852-862
  @case 'moves: every pitch a move, and every move\'s inversion beside it'  [pure]  @ 866-876
  @case 'moves: two pitches naming one interval are one move'  [pure]  @ 880-888
  @case 'moves: simplest first, the last move stating the complexity bound'  [pure]  @ 892-908
  @case 'moves: a temper holding a pitch that is not a ratio is no move set'  [pure]  @ 912-917
  @case 'stepClass: an exact octave shares a class, and nothing else does'  [pure]  @ 921-947
  @case 'noteStep: an intent names the step a note has been moved off'  [pure]  @ 951-975
  @case 'seatWindow: a note at either edge of its window still reads as its own step'  [pure]  @ 979-1005
  @case 'shortlist: the key step holds the unison, and the tonic does not move'  [pure]  @ 1009-1027
  @case 'shortlist: the rival spellings of a step, nearest first'  [pure]  @ 1031-1047
  @case 'shortlist: the hole at the tritone is the target\'s, not the step\'s'  [pure]  @ 1051-1062
  @case 'shortlist: widened, the hole reaches the nearest points either side'  [pure]  @ 1066-1081
  @case 'shortlist: an unequal notation strains by the side the point lies on'  [pure]  @ 1085-1097
  @case 'shortlist: one window serves the strand, in every register'  [pure]  @ 1101-1125

